Ok.. we basically figured that this is the deal with Eternal 
City right now:
 
Linear Paths from Eternal City to other areas:
 - Africa                  - Nargolia        - Doom
 - Aeschbourne             - Videopolis      - MoeTown [tm]
 - Castle Drakmoor, etc..  - Bard Castle     - Ragnarok
 
Trans Objects:
 - History of Eternal City  - Fish Pond      - Amos Trask's Ship
 - Warp Transphere          - Sand Pit       - X-Men jet
 - Atlantis whirlpool       - "R" dispenser  - Resort Bus
 - Gem to Riddler's Quest
 
Moving Trans Items:
 - Fred        - Elven horse    - Magic Pizza Hut 
 
Locations in Eternal City:
 - Heart               - A&A Clothiers       - Adventurer's G.H.
 - Anarchy Interdim.   - Bed & Breakfast     - Dr.F's Body Shop
 - Dave's Throne Room  - Eight Ball          - Everything Inc.
 - FU-Union-Lounge     - Library             - Oracle
 - Paranoid C&A        - Sivar's Hall        - Eternal S&L
 - Temple of the Ages  - Temple of Eternity  - Tower of Wizardry
 - Warrior Guild       - Videopolis          - Snapperhead Bar & Grill
 
And of course the Lounge and associated rooms..
 
  Now picture this, if you will..  The Eternal City is 
actually up on a plateau-resembling thing, with as much of 
EotL as we can spread out around it in a straight-forward sort 
of way.  The idea of doing this is to cut down on the number 
of just plain "alternate dimensions" or whatever, and make the 
areas of the mud a little more cohesive in how they relate to 
each other.  Basically, you should be able to walk to just 
about anywhere on the mud.  
  Here's the picture for how that's laid out..  Let's start 
with Eternal City itself first.  As many of you may already 
know, Eternal City is cluttered.  Cluttered with wierd trans 
items and exits that simply don't make logical sense.  Figure 
that the only real essential parts of EC are these..
 
                        A MAP OF ETERNAL CITY
                                        Points of Interest
                                        ==================
               SL    PCA          *: Heart of E.C.
               |      |         AAC: A&A Clothiers
          BB-r-r-r-r--r--r--r    AI: Anarchy Interdim.                          
             |     |        |    BB: Bed & Breakfast     
             r  AI-r     EI-r    BS: Dr.F's Body Shop                     
             |     |            DTR: Dave's Throne Room                       
       AAC   r-BS  r-V           EI: Everything Inc.                     
        |    |     |             FU: FU-Union-Lounge                    
    r-r-r--r-*-r-r-r            LIB: E.C. Library        
    | |    | |                    O: Oracle                     
   TA r O LI r                  PCA: Paranoid C&A                        
      | |    |                   SL: Eternal S&L                      
  DTR-r-r--r-r                   TA: Temple of the Ages                       
      |      |                   TE: Temple of Eternity            
      r-TE  FU                    V: Videopolis
                                  r: road                  
                                                   
  Now as you can see from this little map thing, I compressed 
the city down a bit and got rid of the guild halls and 
non-working bits.  This was just a quick change though, and 
the future map of EC would probably be worked out by a group 
of people or someone who spends some actual time working into 
it an ease of accessibility for first time players.  Another 
thing which was changed that you can't tell in the diagram, is 
that all of the trans items and routes to different areas are 
gone.  
  Did you ever find it strange that you could be standing on a 
busy street in a bustling metropolis, go one room west, and 
suddenly find yourself on a grassy hill with 2 castles in 
plain sight?  It's a transition like this that leads to 
inconsistancy in the mud.  Now some may argue that one of the 
appealing bits to EotL is the whole chaotic, melting-pot-of-
genres style of gaming.  I'm not refuting that.  I AM, on the 
other hand, pointing out that there is a serious problem when 
the reasons these inconsistencies are not explained to the 
players.  
  In any event, here's the thought.  Eternal City will 
be on say, a plateu in  |        / \  ----------
the middle of an island.|        \ /   ^ ^ ^ ^ ^  \
The "edges" of the city |        /      ^_^__ ^     \ <- Island
will be said to be at   | Urban |       |    |       |
the points where the    |  |    |___    | EC |    @ @|
cliffs of this plateau  |  `--->|__  \  |____| @ @ @ |  Ocean
drop off.  We could then|    ,-->\  \  \    @ @ @ @ /
have 4 or 5 gates which | Transit \ |  |    @ @ @/
would allow access to   |             ----------
the base of the plateau.  Once at the base of the plateau, 
players would still be in the Eternal cabal area, but it 
would become a bit more challenging.. possible wandering 
monsters, mini-quests, who knows.  The idea is that players 
will then be able to walk to areas, or take trans items 
that take them along the surface of the world so that there 
can be a sense of geographical spatial relationships.  I'll 
just list which ways the areas will go, by listing what 
slice of the island is doing what..
 
 - In the 12 o'clock position, a small mountain range was 
suggested, which could, upon crossing it, take you to Nargolia,
Ragnarok, and the whole Shrine/Chaos/Orc Quest place, via 
separate paths, of course.
 
 - At about 1:30-ish, the idea was to have a staircase 
constructed of musical notes or something (Music cabal's 
choice) that would take you up into the Bard Castle area.  We 
figured that since it was a quasi-surreal area anyways, then 
it would help out the geography to just change the altitude of 
the area.
 
 - From 3 to 6, we were thinkin' of having a large forest, 
with twisting paths and all that sort of standard forest 
stuff, as well as the little area of the village Aescbourne 
(Forests cabal) which could simply be completely contained 
within this forest.  
 
 - From 6 to 9-ish we thought that an urban area would be 
kinda cool, with an airport/mass transit center at the heart 
of it.  The urban area could easily have Fred wandering around 
inside of it and fit the Vagabond/Trask area (wherever the heck 
it is now)in it.  The transit center could give helicopter 
rides to MoeTown, bus rides to the resort, and X-Men access 
via their jet thing, all which should be explained as being on 
other islands.
 
 - At straight 9 o'clock would be the whole Castle Drakmoor/
Draconian Reach hulaballoo, since its area extends to the 
north and west of its entrance area.  It would be accessible 
by a sturdy bridge of some sort.
 
 - And lastly, at 10:30 we'd have some sort of dock area, where 
various boats and ferries would take you to Elfland, Riftwar, 
and Africa, not to mention a scuba gear shop or something to 
get to Atlantis.
 
  - We could fit the Castle of Doom and Citadel areas just 
about anywhere, since their entry objects are indicated as 
being tears in space of some sort.
 
  - The Elven Horse and the Magic Pizza Hut would both stay 
wandering through EC as they are.
 
  Anyways, this is an idea that we think can work, and will 
add to the whole "suspension of disbelief" bit, because 
players can envision more of the mud as being spread out on a 
map.  Anyways, that's just our $5,526.87 .  We'll try to draw 
up some maps, and if you have anything to add, just tack it 
on the end or make another doc or somethin'..



Appendation:  The new EC map is in /zone/null/eternal/NEW/city/MAP 
             and an updated version of this document will shortly 
             take its place once we can whip one out.
